          "phase": "final_answer",
          "text": "Boredom alone would probably feel too slight to carry a deliberate risk to his life. It can explain why he becomes curious, but the reader needs to understand why getting this letter matters more to him than staying safe.\n\nOne alternative: he believes the letter offers a chance to put right a harm he caused. That gives the risk an emotional cost: walking away would mean leaving that harm unresolved.\n\nBoth motives remain proposals. The life-risking retrieval is also unestablished, and the earlier letter and childhood ideas stay undecided."
